On this page, you will need to introduce your worklog. How did you complete it? How many weeks did you take to complete the program? What did you do in those weeks?
Typically, and as a standard, a worklog is carried out over about 3 months (throughout the internship period) with weekly contents as follows:
Week 1: GMaster the foundations of AWS account administration &amp; security (IAM, cost management, support), understand and deploy a basic network infrastructure (VPC), get familiar with cloud development environments (Cloud9), and set up static web hosting and relational databases (S3, RDS)
Week 2: Expand knowledge in simplified compute (Lightsail), system scalability &amp; monitoring (Auto Scaling, CloudWatch), advanced networking (Route 53, Networking Workshop, Windows workloads), NoSQL &amp; caching (DynamoDB, ElastiCache), and complete the foundation with CDN and high-availability architecture
Week 3: - Hold team meetings to discuss, propose, and finalize the topic for the individual project. Develop ideas and ensure the topic solves a practical problem on AWS. Research and select a suitable infrastructure architecture (preferably Serverless) to build the system. Complete the proposal with a clear technological direction and development roadmap. Visualize the solution using detailed architecture diagrams. Prepare the source code environment and troubleshoot issues related to the project template (Git submodule errors)
Week 4: Master Serverless fundamentals (Lambda, SQS, IAM Role) and independently implement Flow 1: Document Processing &amp; Storage
Week 5: Build a secure communication gateway for end users, connect retrieval from OpenSearch, and implement Semantic Cache to optimize Bedrock invocation costs
Week 6: Prevent the system from running &ldquo;blind&rdquo; — detect incidents immediately, distinguish between minor and critical errors, and route alerts to the right channel (Slack) for timely operational response. Implement automated RAG quality evaluation using the RAGAS framework (Faithfulness, Answer Relevancy, Context Precision) via EventBridge Scheduler and Lambda Evaluation Runner
Week 7: Review all 4 system flows from a holistic perspective, resolve coarse edges identified in previous weeks (especially retrieval quality), write operational documentation, and deliver the official project demo to the team/mentor
